{
  "_README": [
    "TRADITIONAL-NAME SHORTENINGS.",
    "",
    "OWNER: seeded with a best-effort starting set, meant to be expanded by",
    "you. Plain data — add an entry and the next `npm run ingest:variants`",
    "picks it up. This is probably the highest-leverage file in the repo to",
    "grow, because these shortenings are the ones a customer actually writes",
    "on a transfer form and no Western matcher knows about.",
    "",
    "Format: 'FULL': ['SHORT', 'SHORT', ...] — all uppercase, no diacritics,",
    "because matching happens on normalised names.",
    "",
    "Note that many of these are NOT prefix or suffix truncations, which is",
    "precisely why edit-distance matching fails on them: CHUKWUEMEKA -> EMEKA",
    "shares no prefix, and Jaro-Winkler in particular weights a common prefix",
    "heavily. The baseline in eval/results.md is measured against exactly this."
  ],
